WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.567
"My gecko is missing!" Mrs. Hubbletree wailed.

2
00:00:07.568 --> 00:00:12.644
"I went to get him from his terrarium, but he is not there!"

3
00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:20.412
"Freaky!" The mayor scanned the gym until he located Mr. Freaky hiding behind a large dog.

4
00:00:20.413 --> 00:00:24.768
"Now, now, Mayor Hubbletree!" Mr. Freaky said quickly.

5
00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:30.335
"I'm sure everything is totally under control!"

6
00:00:30.336 --> 00:00:35.560
A judge went over to Mrs. Hubbletree.

7
00:00:35.561 --> 00:00:39.666
"Rainbow geckos can change color," the judge said calmly.

8
00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:45.271
"Maybe Bowie is simply blending into his terrarium."

9
00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:51.154
"Are you saying my wife can't find her own pet?" Mayor Hubbletree demanded.

10
00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:56.428
Mrs. Hubbletree shook her head. "I looked carefully," she insisted.

11
00:00:56.429 --> 00:00:59.951
"Somebody stole my precious Bowie!"

12
00:00:59.952 --> 00:01:04.467
"Lock down this place immediately!" Mayor Hubbletree shouted.

13
00:01:04.468 --> 00:01:10.223
"Nobody gets in or out until Bowie is found!"

14
00:01:10.224 --> 00:01:12.699
Miss Bungle hurried toward the microphone.

15
00:01:12.707 --> 00:01:15.530
"There's no need for panic.

16
00:01:15.531 --> 00:01:23.262
We're going to check our security camera to see if we can spot any suspicious activity near the gecko's terrarium.

17
00:01:23.263 --> 00:01:27.907
We'll also check to see if anyone suspicious recently left the building."

18
00:01:27.908 --> 00:01:31.232
"What are you talking about?" Mayor Hubbletree yelled.

19
00:01:31.233 --> 00:01:35.460
"This place is crawling with vampires, ghosts, and ghouls.

20
00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:38.347
Half the crowd looks suspicious!"

21
00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:41.338
Ben and Winnie exchanged nervous glances.

22
00:01:41.339 --> 00:01:48.328
"This is getting totally out of control," Ben murmured.

23
00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:53.953
"Students, do not take action by yourselves," Miss Bungle added.

24
00:01:53.954 --> 00:02:00.266
"If you spot anything unusual, notify me or Mr. Freaky immediately."

25
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.686
"This is terrible," Ben said.

26
00:02:02.687 --> 00:02:07.970
"Poor Mrs. Hubbletree. I wish we could do something."

27
00:02:07.971 --> 00:02:11.568
"I could cast a location spell," Waldo said.

28
00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:14.676
"No!" Ben and Winnie said at once.

29
00:02:14.677 --> 00:02:18.649
"I bet Rex-Rex could sniff out Bowie," Mog said.

30
00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.673
"Hey, that's a good idea!" Ben said.

31
00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.054
"Rex-Rex could pick up his scent."

32
00:02:24.055 --> 00:02:28.994
"We just need to find something that belongs to Bowie," Mog said.

33
00:02:28.995 --> 00:02:32.752
"Oswald can look for him too," Waldo reached for Oswald's cage.

34
00:02:32.753 --> 00:02:36.444
"No!" Winnie and Ben said again.

35
00:02:36.445 --> 00:02:42.432
"Let's go!" Mog said, bringing Rex-Rex over to Bowie's terrarium for a good sniff.

36
00:02:42.433 --> 00:02:50.305
Almost immediately, Rex-Rex took off, dragging Mog all over the school as he sniffed.

37
00:02:50.306 --> 00:02:57.049
Ben hurried after them. "How's it going?" he asked a few minutes later.

38
00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:03.666
Mog shrugged. "It seems like Rex-Rex smells him everywhere. Maybe—"

39
00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:09.646
"Shh." Ben pointed to Miss Bungle who was about to make another announcement.

40
00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:11.047
"Maybe they found him."

41
00:03:11.048 --> 00:03:13.052
But Bowie was still missing.

42
00:03:13.053 --> 00:03:20.711
"After checking the camera," Miss Bungle began, "we believe Bowie is still in the building.

43
00:03:20.712 --> 00:03:22.873
But we need help with our search.

44
00:03:22.874 --> 00:03:30.237
Can all of the pet show volunteers please step up to the stage?"

45
00:03:30.238 --> 00:03:34.564
Sid grinned. "We get to be security guards!"

46
00:03:34.565 --> 00:03:38.092
Ben nodded. "Let's go, Sid."

47
00:03:38.093 --> 00:03:44.276
Ben and Sid searched some classrooms on the first floor and the cafeteria.

48
00:03:44.277 --> 00:03:46.624
"Bowie can change color," Ben said.

49
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:50.227
"He could be blending in anywhere."

50
00:03:50.228 --> 00:03:58.364
After about half an hour, they gave up and reentered the gym.

51
00:03:58.365 --> 00:04:03.506
"Uh-oh," Ben said. He saw Mayor Hubbletree glaring at Waldo.

52
00:04:03.507 --> 00:04:06.251
The ghosts hurried over.

53
00:04:06.252 --> 00:04:10.491
"We demand to search that cage!" the mayor snapped.

54
00:04:10.492 --> 00:04:15.296
"Your owl tried to eat the witch's kitten," Mrs. Hubbletree added.

55
00:04:15.297 --> 00:04:18.185
"I think it ate Bowie too!"

56
00:04:18.186 --> 00:04:22.020
"Oswald hasn't eaten anyone!" Waldo protested.

57
00:04:22.021 --> 00:04:27.703
"Take your pet out of that cage right now!" Mayor Hubbletree ordered.

58
00:04:27.704 --> 00:04:29.428
"Show him to me!"

59
00:04:29.429 --> 00:04:36.036
Waldo sighed. "As I just said, Mayor Hubbletree, my owl is invisible.

60
00:04:36.037 --> 00:04:38.346
So I can't show him to you."

61
00:04:38.347 --> 00:04:43.383
"We want to see for ourselves!" the mayor demanded.

62
00:04:43.384 --> 00:04:46.576
"Fine!" Waldo said. "I'll show you what—"

63
00:04:46.577 --> 00:04:51.919
He opened the cage and reached inside. "Uh-oh."

64
00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:57.063
Ben gulped. "What's wrong, Waldo?"

65
00:04:57.064 --> 00:04:59.656
"Oswald escaped again!"

66
00:04:59.657 --> 00:05:05.434
Mrs. Hubbletree gasped and Mayor Hubbletree's face turned bright red.

67
00:05:05.435 --> 00:05:10.250
"Are you telling me that your owl is loose?"

68
00:05:10.251 --> 00:05:15.367
"Oswald hasn't actually hurt anyone," Ben said quickly. "Inky is fine, and—"

69
00:05:15.368 --> 00:05:22.289
Tears streamed down Mrs. Hubbletree's cheeks. "My poor Bowie!" she sobbed.

70
00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:26.733
"Why did I ever think that he would be safe here?"

71
00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:31.155
"Now, now, dear." Mayor Hubbletree patted his wife's shoulder.

72
00:05:31.156 --> 00:05:34.546
"We'll find your precious Bowie."

73
00:05:34.547 --> 00:05:37.298
"Call Oswald, Waldo," Ben said.

74
00:05:37.299 --> 00:05:43.553
Waldo shrugged and whistled twice sharply. "Oswald, turn visible!"

75
00:05:43.554 --> 00:05:47.486
Ben held his breath as he looked upward.

76
00:05:47.487 --> 00:05:53.621
There was no sign of the owl until a fish monster shouted and pointed to the scoreboard.

77
00:05:53.622 --> 00:05:55.531
"There he is!"

78
00:05:55.532 --> 00:05:59.596
Waldo held out an arm and whistled again.

79
00:05:59.597 --> 00:06:03.865
This time the owl flew down and landed on Waldo's hand.

80
00:06:03.866 --> 00:06:06.688
"Good boy!" Waldo said.

81
00:06:06.689 --> 00:06:12.618
"He is not a good boy!" Mrs. Hubbletree said. "He stole my gecko!"

82
00:06:12.619 --> 00:06:14.658
Mayor Hubbletree looked grim.

83
00:06:14.659 --> 00:06:21.301
"I know where we'll find your gecko—inside that dangerous owl's stomach!"

84
00:06:21.302 --> 00:06:27.512
Mrs. Hubbletree gasped. "Are you saying what I think you're saying?"

85
00:06:27.513 --> 00:06:30.332
"Yes!" the mayor replied.

86
00:06:30.333 --> 00:06:36.288
"That's exactly what I'm saying—we're going to cut open that owl!"

